From a4d83c62bd9f8b7f4c1d2ce905db8785308b2501 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 11:24:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: sun50i-h616: propagate audio hub rate changes

The audio hub clock is a mux and a power of two divider fed by the audio
PLL. Without CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT its consumer can only pick between the
rates the PLL happens to run at, which is not enough to switch between
the 44.1 kHz and 48 kHz families, or to reach the bit clock a high bit
rate HDMI stream needs.

Let rate requests propagate to the parent, like the I2S clocks on H6 do.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
index 955c614830fa..ae8bdd5528e1 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
@@ -566,7 +566,7 @@ static struct ccu_div audio_hub_clk = {
 		.hw.init	= CLK_HW_INIT_PARENTS("audio-hub",
 						      audio_parents,
 						      &ccu_div_ops,
-						      0),
+						      CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT),
 	},
 };
 
